  "structure": "Ten required 6 EC units in each of years one and two. In year three, 30 EC of open elective study, three 6 EC choices out of seven and a 12 EC thesis. BRIDGE has zero credits, and the 30 EC honours track is additional. No course from either is counted in the 180 EC. The degree chart and annual module guide control over the condensed recruitment overview.",
  "progression": "The 2026–2027 pathway totals 180 EC: ten compulsory 6 EC courses in each of Years 1 and 2, 30 EC open study, three selected 6 EC subjects from seven, and a 12 EC thesis. The retained electives are Econometrics III, Machine Learning for Econometrics and Data Science, and Fair, Transparent and Interpretable Machine Learning; they are choices, not universal requirements. There is no formal graduation route. Teaching is English, with Dutch tutorial/expression/exam-answer options in Years 1–2. BSA requires 42 first-year EC, a pass in Calculus/Analysis I OR Analysis II/Mathematical Reasoning AND a pass in Introduction to Data Science OR Statistics. The English diagnostic or refresher gates Data Analysis I. Zero-credit BRIDGE requires attendance at five of six plenaries. Data Science Practical requires a final Data Structures and Algorithms grade of at least 5.5, or a first-period partial grade of at least 5.5 in Econometrics I or Numerical Methods. Thesis entry requires120EC including minor and at least two passes from Econometrics II, Multivariate Statistics and Data Science Methods. The thesis is individual quantitative research with a paper and poster/presentation, assessed by supervisor and second reader; topics appear in Period4. The current July2027 diploma deadline concerns current final-year students, not the future Fall2026 entrant’s Year3. The minor normally requires90EC; open study has at most6EC level100, at least12EC level300 and no compulsory-course overlap. Prior board approval applies except stated faculty/university/Education-minor exemptions; the Economics university minor is prohibited for EDS. Course manuals may require attendance. Honours is additional and excluded. Visible adopted OER AppendixVII schedule, version26-2-2026, is controlling; recruitment SAM and shortened elective list are outdated/incomplete. The annual Introduction to Data Science course is probability theory, not UCR-style data cleaning. Current year verified in each annual course page. No outgoing edition or guessed future deadline is used.",
  "interestAccounting": "Reviewed all 35 exact rows, nine direct interests, 15 curricular topics, two illustrations and nine outcomes or trajectories. Application questions remain tied to the direct interests, while the illustrative and career rows serve as context.",
